-- Generated by `pnpm db:generate --name=unique_service_name`, then annotated by
-- hand BEFORE it was ever applied anywhere. Once a migration has run, it is frozen.
--
-- Note what this statement costs: CREATE INDEX takes a SHARE lock on the table,
-- which blocks INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE for as long as the index build takes. On an
-- empty or small table that is microseconds. On a production table with millions
-- of rows it is an outage, and the fix is:
--     CREATE UNIQUE INDEX CONCURRENTLY "services_name_uq" ON "services" ("name");
-- CONCURRENTLY cannot run inside a transaction block, so it needs a migration of
-- its own and care with Drizzle's statement-splitting marker.
--
-- (Careful: Drizzle's migrator splits a .sql file on the literal marker comment
-- it writes between statements. Never let that exact token appear inside prose,
-- not even inside a comment — it will cut your file in half. Ask me how I know.)
CREATE UNIQUE INDEX "services_name_uq" ON "services" USING btree ("name");
